        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-kernel_channels_order_completely",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "KERNEL.ORG'S CHANNELS, COMPARED COMPLETELY: the eight versioned release lines (mainline, stable, longterm-6.18, longterm-6.12, longterm-6.6, longterm-6.1, longterm-5.15, longterm-5.10), each encoded losslessly as major·10⁶ + minor·10³ + patch, order STRICTLY over all 28 pairs — not adjacent samples, every pair (the one-step-is-not-a-walk law): mainline above stable above the six longterm lines in their own strict descent. The versions are kernel.org's published releases.json data; the completeness is the kernel's."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "(List.range 8).all (fun i => (List.range 8).all (fun j => Nat.ble j i || nth [7002000, 7001009, 6018045, 6012104, 6006152, 6001183, 5015216, 5010265] i > nth [7002000, 7001009, 6018045, 6012104, 6006152, 6001183, 5015216, 5010265] j))"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem kernel_channels_order_completely : (List.range 8).all (fun i => (List.range 8).all (fun j => Nat.ble j i || nth [7002000, 7001009, 6018045, 6012104, 6006152, 6001183, 5015216, 5010265] i > nth [7002000, 7001009, 6018045, 6012104, 6006152, 6001183, 5015216, 5010265] j)) := by decide"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-version_encoding_is_lossless",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "THE ENCODING ROUND-TRIPS ON ITS DOMAIN: every encoded version splits back exactly — major = e/10⁶, minor = (e/10³) mod 10³, patch = e mod 10³ — because every published minor and patch sits under 1000. Losslessness is what makes the total order MEAN version order: the software wing's split-and-recompose law, applied to the kernel's own numbering."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "([7002000, 7001009, 6018045, 6012104, 6006152, 6001183, 5015216, 5010265] : List Nat).all (fun e => (e / 1000000) * 1000000 + ((e / 1000) % 1000) * 1000 + (e % 1000) = e ∧ (e / 1000) % 1000 < 1000 ∧ e % 1000 < 1000)"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem version_encoding_is_lossless : ([7002000, 7001009, 6018045, 6012104, 6006152, 6001183, 5015216, 5010265] : List Nat).all (fun e => (e / 1000000) * 1000000 + ((e / 1000) % 1000) * 1000 + (e % 1000) = e ∧ (e / 1000) % 1000 < 1000 ∧ e % 1000 < 1000) := by decide"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-register_ladder_doubles_completely",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "THE PROMOTION CHAIN, COMPARED WHOLE: the register ladder 4 → 8 → 16 → 32 → 64 → 128 (hexbit, pair, coin-half, address-half, coin, address) doubles COMPLETELY — every one of the 15 pairs, not just neighbours, satisfies W[j] = W[i]·2^(j−i): any two registers on the ladder are an EXACT number of coin-payments apart. The fold-to-zero promotion, quantified over all pairs at once."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "(List.range 6).all (fun i => (List.range 6).all (fun j => Nat.ble j i || nth [4, 8, 16, 32, 64, 128] j = nth [4, 8, 16, 32, 64, 128] i * 2 ^ (j - i)))"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem register_ladder_doubles_completely : (List.range 6).all (fun i => (List.range 6).all (fun j => Nat.ble j i || nth [4, 8, 16, 32, 64, 128] j = nth [4, 8, 16, 32, 64, 128] i * 2 ^ (j - i))) := by decide"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-the_surface_is_the_geometric_mean",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "THE JEWEL: the pressure ladder in sixtieths (diver at 3 atm = 180, at 2 atm = 120, THE SURFACE = 60, the astronaut's suit near 1/3 atm = 20) orders completely — and the buddy depths MULTIPLY to the surface squared: 180·20 = 3600 = 60². The shared world every diver ascends to and every astronaut descends to is the GEOMETRIC MEAN of their two exiles — the mandala's still center, reached by multiplication: the two hands of the pressure column close on the same 60 the harmonic sixtieths walk."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "((List.range 4).all (fun i => (List.range 4).all (fun j => Nat.ble j i || nth [180, 120, 60, 20] i > nth [180, 120, 60, 20] j))) ∧ (180 * 20 = 3600) ∧ (60 * 60 = 3600) ∧ (120 * 30 = 3600)"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem the_surface_is_the_geometric_mean : ((List.range 4).all (fun i => (List.range 4).all (fun j => Nat.ble j i || nth [180, 120, 60, 20] i > nth [180, 120, 60, 20] j))) ∧ (180 * 20 = 3600) ∧ (60 * 60 = 3600) ∧ (120 * 30 = 3600) := by decide"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
